From 7501d654c08231fd89562caa66da6b25b27c9461 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:10:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): a probe searches a short way past the face and
 feeds below the safe plane

Found on a real Tormach 770MX (#521's hands-on test): a new Probe op
searched 5 mm past the expected face (G38.2 Z-0.1969), deep enough to
bottom a stylus when the face is missing, and rapided straight down to
the approach point over the part.

- A new Probe op's probe distance is max(2 x tolerance, 1 mm) (1 mm for
  the seeded tolerance); existing documents keep their stated value.
- A probe distance past 2 mm draws a named, non-blocking
  Warning::ProbeSearch (the post is not held).
- The probe cycle opens with a positioning rapid that ends at the safe
  plane, then FEEDS down to the approach point: no probe rapid runs
  below the safe plane. Fanuc probe goldens gain that line.
- The probe page's hint says the distance is a search limit, not a
  destination.

Pinned by probe_search (3 tests; below_the_safe_plane_a_probe_only_feeds
fails on the old cycle).

Fixes #570

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
